0014: a mutable image with no format list keeps the tiled layout of its texel
block.

Status: DRAFT - not built and not run. The p14 release shipped the other form
of this change (enumerating a compatibility class and passing a synthesized
list); that form is what tag 27.0.0-devel-p14 and the release's source bundle
contain. This file replaces it on this branch. The gate before it ships is at
the end.

Why. A VkImageCreateInfo with VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT and no
VkImageFormatListCreateInfo may be viewed as any format compatible with its
base format, but the driver does not know which, so the predicates in
tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear() are handed a NULL and answer the worst
case: has_swaps true, reinterprets_r8g8_r16 true, swaps_are_uniform false. The
image goes linear although every format the app may legally view it as has the
same layout. Not a corner case: 50.9% of the sampled texture bytes in the RE4
inventory (results/raw/game-patched-imginv4.log) are MUTABLE with listn=0 and
all of them are linear.

The rule. An absent list means "any format with the same texel block", and the
tiled layout is a function of the block alone, so the question is whether two
members of one block describe different memory. They do in exactly one class,
the 2-byte one:

  - A stored tiled image carries no channel order. fd6_pipe2swap()
    (fdl/fd6_format_table.c) returns WZYX for every tiled format that is not
    is_mutable - "It seems CCU ignores swap and always uses WZYX when tiled.
    TP, on the other hand, always respects swap" - and a view is programmed
    with its own format, so an R8G8B8A8 image read through a B8G8R8A8 view is
    the reinterpretation the spec describes, not a layout disagreement. The
    comment at this same decision in tu_image_init() says it too ("tiled
    images are stored without the swap") and leaves a TODO about BGRA8.
  - UBWC is already off for such an image: there is no list to judge
    compression against, so tu_image_init() clears ubwc_enabled in this
    branch. The swap is only a problem once compressed, which is what the two
    predicates below the new one are for.
  - The 2-byte class is the exception, and it is a layout fact rather than an
    order one: R8G8 has a tile height and a pitch alignment of its own, and
    fdl/fd6_layout.c keeps that variant only while the image is not flagged
    is_mutable ("cpp == 2 && nr_components == 2 && !is_mutable"). A part
    without ubwc_all_formats_compatible never sets that flag on A7xx, so an
    R8G8 image cannot be reinterpreted as R16 in the layout it gets. The
    answer for an absent list is the r8g8 question and nothing else.

What changes. Two files:

  - tu_formats.cc: after the depth/stencil, NV12 and ubwc_all_formats_compatible
    cases of tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear(), an absent or empty list
    returns tu_is_r8g8_compatible(base format) instead of falling through to
    the swap predicates. The comment at the call site in
    tu_get_image_format_properties(), which used to say a query without a list
    "cannot know this", now says the opposite: the same predicate answers for
    the base format, so the query cannot promise a combination the create
    would refuse.
  - tu_image.cc: the create-side branch spelled the same three predicates
    inline. It now calls the function the query calls, so the two cannot drift
    apart. UBWC stays cleared in that branch, as before.

This deliberately does not touch device props. The other way to answer this
question is info->props.ubwc_all_formats_compatible, which is the A750 feature
bit: it makes every part mutable at the layout level and is read by the sparse
residency gate as well (tu_formats.cc). It measured broken on A740 - garbage
cast reads - see docs/a7xx-gen-props.md row 23 and
results/test-props-ubwc_all_formats_compatible.log, so it stays off here and
the answer comes from the texel block instead.

Relations. Depends on 0005 (the swap predicates this patch stops using for the
no-list case) and on nothing else. Independent of 0013.

Gate, before this is fit to ship. One thing has never been measured: a read
through a view whose format is a different member of the base format's block
class, on a tiled image with UBWC off. v1 did not measure it either - its own
header says so. tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c is extended with that probe: a
B8G8R8A8 MUTABLE image with no list, filled through 0013's buffer->image path,
read back through an R8G8B8A8 view (expect the R and B bytes exchanged) and an
R32_UINT view (expect the raw word), both through the TP path because
vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer reads with the image format, not the view's. The guard
case has to stay refused: R16 over R8G8 must still be linear. Then the 94-check
matrix, then the RE4 inventory; the expected gain is the 4-byte class, about
1600 MiB of the 3801 MiB that p14's v1 left in linear.

Not built, not run. `git apply --check` passes for 0001-0014 on Mesa
`6dfa32a85f91` with no --3way and no fuzz. The device is the test bench and its
build script refuses to start while re4.exe runs, so no compile was attempted.
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_formats.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_formats.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_formats.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_formats.cc
@@ -288,6 +288,29 @@ tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear(const struct fd_dev_info *info,
    if (info->props.ubwc_all_formats_compatible)
       return false;
 
+   /* Without a list the image may be viewed as any format with the same texel
+    * block, and the tiled layout is a function of the block alone.  A stored
+    * tiled image carries no channel order: fd6_pipe2swap() returns WZYX for
+    * every tiled format that is not is_mutable ("CCU ignores swap and always
+    * uses WZYX when tiled", fdl/fd6_format_table.c), and a view decodes with
+    * its own format, so two members of one block class describe the same
+    * bytes.  Reading one as the other is the reinterpretation the spec
+    * describes, not a layout disagreement.
+    *
+    * UBWC is off for such an image - there is no list to judge compression
+    * against - and that is the only case in which the swap mattered, which is
+    * what the predicates below are for.
+    *
+    * The one block class whose members do not share a layout is the 2-byte
+    * one: R8G8 has a tile height and a pitch alignment of its own, and the
+    * layout keeps that variant only while the image is not flagged is_mutable
+    * (fdl/fd6_layout.c: "cpp == 2 && nr_components == 2 && !is_mutable"),
+    * which a part without ubwc_all_formats_compatible never sets.  So the
+    * answer for an absent list is the r8g8 question and nothing else.
+    */
+   if (!fmt_list || !fmt_list->viewFormatCount)
+      return tu_is_r8g8_compatible(vk_format_to_pipe_format(format));
+
    if (tu6_format_list_reinterprets_r8g8_r16(vk_format_to_pipe_format(format),
                                              fmt_list))
       return true;
@@ -809,8 +832,9 @@ tu_get_image_format_properties(
 
       /* Same for a mutable image whose format list demotes it to linear: the
        * create is refused (see tu_image_init()), so don't advertise the
-       * combination here either.  A query without a format list cannot know
-       * this, and stays as it is.
+       * combination here either.  Without a list the same predicate answers
+       * for the compatibility class of the base format, so the query cannot
+       * promise a combination the create would refuse.
        */
       if (info->flags & VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT) {
          const VkImageFormatListCreateInfo *format_list =
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
@@ -593,12 +593,12 @@ tu_image_init(struct tu_device *device, struct tu_image *image,
                ubwc_enabled = false;
             }
 
-            bool r8g8_r16 = tu6_format_list_reinterprets_r8g8_r16(vk_format_to_pipe_format(image->vk.format), fmt_list);
-            bool fmt_list_has_swaps = tu6_format_list_has_swaps(fmt_list);
-
-            if (r8g8_r16 ||
-                (fmt_list_has_swaps &&
-                 !tu6_format_list_swaps_are_uniform(fmt_list))) {
+            /* The predicate the format query uses, spelled once: the create
+             * and what vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2 advertised
+             * cannot drift apart this way.
+             */
+            if (tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear(
+                   device->physical_device->info, image->vk.format, fmt_list)) {
                ubwc_enabled = false;
                force_linear_tile = true;
             }
